Face Detection & Segregation (Unsupervised Learning Version):
-> This project is an unsupervised system for face grouping and organization.
-> Instead of training a classifier with labeled reference images, it automatically clusters faces based on similarity — no manual labeling required.
-> It uses MTCNN (for face detection) and InceptionResnetV1 (FaceNet) (for face embeddings), then applies unsupervised algorithms (like K-Means, DBSCAN, or Agglomerative Clustering) to group similar faces together.

Who Can Use This?
This version is ideal for:
-> People who want to automatically group large photo collections by person without manually labeling images.
-> Researchers or students studying unsupervised representation learning and clustering-based image organization.
-> Archivists or photographers who want to discover recurring faces automatically.

Quick Summary (Gist):
You only need:
1. A folder in Google Drive with input photos (mixed people, events, or collections).
2. The notebook (face_segregation_unsupervised.ipynb) in Google Colab.
3. The code automatically detects faces, computes embeddings, and groups similar faces.
4. The output will be a folder in Drive structured as:
/output_clustered/
 ├── cluster_0/
 ├── cluster_1/
 ├── cluster_2/
 └── ...

Each folder represents a unique person or group of visually similar faces.

Step-by-Step Setup (Google Colab):
1. Install Required Libraries
Run this cell first in Colab:

!pip uninstall -y pillow
!pip install pillow==9.5.0 --force-reinstall
!pip install facenet-pytorch==2.5.3
!pip install -q torch torchvision matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn opencv-python-headless pandas

2. Mount Google Drive

from google.colab import drive
drive.mount('/content/drive')

Your files will appear under /content/drive/MyDrive/.

3. Folder Structure in Google Drive
Create a project folder like this:

/MyDrive/face_project_unsupervised/
 ├── input_photos/
 │    ├── photo1.jpg
 │    ├── photo2.jpg
 │    └── ...
 └── output_clustered/   ← (This will be automatically created)

4. Update Configuration Paths in Code
Edit these paths in your notebook before running:

input_path = "/content/drive/MyDrive/face_project_unsupervised/input_photos"
CFG = {
    "image_size": 160,
    "blur_threshold": 80,
    "output_dir": "/content/drive/MyDrive/face_project_unsupervised/output_clustered",
    "cluster_method": "dbscan",   # or "kmeans", "agglomerative"
    "min_samples": 2,
    "eps": 0.7
}

5. Run the Clustering Step
Once the setup is done, execute the main clustering cell.
The notebook will:
-> Detect faces in all input photos.
-> Compute embeddings using FaceNet (512-D feature vectors).
-> Apply the selected unsupervised clustering algorithm.
-> Create folders (cluster_0, cluster_1, …) and copy similar faces there.

6. Visual Summary
At the end, the notebook automatically displays:
-> A bar chart showing how many faces were found per cluster.
-> Optionally, a representative face image for each cluster.

